# Cloud SQL Admin Operations

**Use Cloud SQL Auth Proxy v2 for all non-interactive SQL execution. There is NO `gcloud sql execute-sql` command.**

## Critical Facts

- **No SQL execution API**: Cloud SQL Admin API is admin-only (instances, users, databases) - NOT SQL execution
- **IPv6 not supported**: Cloud SQL Gen2 only supports IPv4; use proxy to avoid connection issues
- **`gcloud sql connect` is interactive only**: Cannot pipe SQL files directly

## Non-Interactive SQL Pattern

```bash
# 1. Download proxy (if needed)
curl -o /tmp/cloud-sql-proxy \
  https://storage.googleapis.com/cloud-sql-connectors/cloud-sql-proxy/v2.11.0/cloud-sql-proxy.darwin.amd64
chmod +x /tmp/cloud-sql-proxy

# 2. Start proxy
/tmp/cloud-sql-proxy --address 127.0.0.1 --port 5433 PROJECT:REGION:INSTANCE &
sleep 5

# 3. Execute SQL non-interactively
PGPASSWORD="$PASSWORD" psql "host=127.0.0.1 port=5433 dbname=DBNAME user=USER sslmode=disable" -f script.sql
# OR inline:
PGPASSWORD="$PASSWORD" psql "host=127.0.0.1 port=5433 dbname=DBNAME user=USER" -c "GRANT ALL ON..."

# 4. Cleanup
pkill -f cloud-sql-proxy
```

## Instance Naming Convention

| Environment | Instance Name | Database |
|-------------|---------------|----------|
| Production | `loist-music-library-db` | `music_library` |
| Staging | `loist-music-library-db-staging` | `loist_mvp_staging` |

## Permission Grants Template

```sql
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE dbname TO username;
\c dbname
GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA public TO username;
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO username;
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON ALL SEQUENCES IN SCHEMA public TO username;
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA public GRANT ALL ON TABLES TO username;
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA public GRANT ALL ON SEQUENCES TO username;
```

## Common Errors

| Error | Cause | Fix |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `[Errno 2] No such file or directory` | Missing `--add-cloudsql-instances` flag | Add flag to Cloud Run deploy |
| `[Errno 5] Input/output error` | Instance doesn't exist or wrong name | Verify instance exists with `gcloud sql instances list` |
| `IPv6 not supported` | Connecting from IPv6 address | Use Cloud SQL Proxy instead |

## Quick Commands

```bash
# List instances
gcloud sql instances list

# List databases on instance
gcloud sql databases list --instance=INSTANCE_NAME

# Create user (password set separately)
gcloud sql users create USERNAME --instance=INSTANCE_NAME --password=PASSWORD

# Set user password
gcloud sql users set-password USERNAME --instance=INSTANCE_NAME --password=PASSWORD
```
